data: {"text":"1. My client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., is a reputed construction company duly incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013,"}

data: {"text":" having its registered office and engaged in the business of civil construction works including road construction, bridge construction, and allied"}

data: {"text":" infrastructure development projects. My client has been actively undertaking various construction projects for Government"}

data: {"text":" departments and has maintained an impeccable track record of timely completion of works"}

data: {"text":" with quality standards.\n\n2. M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd. was awarded a contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No. BRCD/PAT/"}

data: {"text":"2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Crores"}

data: {"text":" Seventy-Five Lakhs only). The said work order was issued by"}

data: {"text":" your office and my client duly accepted the same and commenced"}

data: {"text":" the construction work as per the terms and conditions stipulated therein.\n\n3. My client diligently executed the"}

data: {"text":" contracted work and completed all the construction activities by 28.02.2026, well within the stipulated time frame. Upon"}

data: {"text":" completion of the work, my client submitted the final running bills along with measurement books duly signed by the site engineer appointed by your department. All form"}

data: {"text":"alities as required under the contract and as per departmental procedures were duly complied with by my client.\n\n4. Despite completion"}

data: {"text":" of the work and submission of all requisite documents, my client made repeated requests and reminders to your office for release"}

data: {"text":" of the final payment. Specifically, reminders were sent on 05.03.2026, 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026, seeking"}

data: {"text":" immediate release of the outstanding payment. However, no positive response has"}

data: {"text":" been received from your end till date.\n\n5. The outstanding final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty-Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only"}

data: {"text":") has remained unpaid since 28.02.2026. This wrongful withholding of payment by your office, despite"}

data: {"text":" completion of work and fulfillment of all contractual obligations by my client, is wholly"}

data: {"text":" unjustified and constitutes a breach of the contractual terms.\n\n6. The non-payment of the legitimate dues has caused severe financial loss and reput"}

data: {"text":"ational damage to my client. My client has been constrained to arrange alternative financing at higher costs to"}

data: {"text":" meet its operational expenses and commitments to suppliers and"}

data: {"text":" workers, thereby suffering substantial monetary loss and hard"}

data: {"text":"ship.\n\n7. In accordance with Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, no suit can be instit"}

data: {"text":"uted against the Government or a public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in his"}

data: {"text":" official capacity until the expiration of two months next after notice in writing has been delivered to or"}

data: {"text":" left at the office of such public officer. This legal notice is being served"}

data: {"text":" in compliance with the said mandatory provision.\n\n8. TAKE"}

data: {"text":" NOTICE that unless the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with interest thereon is released within two"}

data: {"text":" months from the date of service of this notice, my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings against you and the State"}

data: {"text":" of Bihar for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages, and costs, without"}

data: {"text":" any further reference to you in the matter."}

