data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908)\n\nDate: 06 May 2026\n\nTo,\nThe Executive Engineer, Bihar Road Construction Department, Government of Bihar\nVishweshwaraiya Bhawan, Bailey Road, Patna - 800015\n\nFrom,\nM/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.\nThrough: Adv. Anjali Verma, Advocate\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Legal Notice under Section 80 CPC — prior to institution of suit against the Government / Public Officer\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., I hereby serve upon you this legal notice under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, and call upon you to note the following:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. My client, M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd., is a reputed construction company duly incorporated under the Companies Act, 2013, having its registered office and engaged in the business of civil construction works including road construction, bridge construction, and allied infrastructure development projects. My client has been actively undertaking various construction projects for Government departments and has maintained an impeccable track record of timely completion of works with quality standards.\n\n2. M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd. was awarded a contract for construction of culverts on NH-31 vide Work Order No. BRCD/PAT/2024/118 dated 12.06.2024 for a total contract value of Rs. 2,75,00,000/- (Rupees Two Crores Seventy-Five Lakhs only). The said work order was issued by your office and my client duly accepted the same and commenced the construction work as per the terms and conditions stipulated therein.\n\n3. My client diligently executed the contracted work and completed all the construction activities by 28.02.2026, well within the stipulated time frame. Upon completion of the work, my client submitted the final running bills along with measurement books duly signed by the site engineer appointed by your department. All formalities as required under the contract and as per departmental procedures were duly complied with by my client.\n\n4. Despite completion of the work and submission of all requisite documents, my client made repeated requests and reminders to your office for release of the final payment. Specifically, reminders were sent on 05.03.2026, 22.03.2026, and 18.04.2026, seeking immediate release of the outstanding payment. However, no positive response has been received from your end till date.\n\n5. The outstanding final payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- (Rupees Eighty-Seven Lakhs Fifty Thousand only) has remained unpaid since 28.02.2026. This wrongful withholding of payment by your office, despite completion of work and fulfillment of all contractual obligations by my client, is wholly unjustified and constitutes a breach of the contractual terms.\n\n6. The non-payment of the legitimate dues has caused severe financial loss and reputational damage to my client. My client has been constrained to arrange alternative financing at higher costs to meet its operational expenses and commitments to suppliers and workers, thereby suffering substantial monetary loss and hardship.\n\n7. In accordance with Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, no suit can be instituted against the Government or a public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done in his official capacity until the expiration of two months next after notice in writing has been delivered to or left at the office of such public officer. This legal notice is being served in compliance with the said mandatory provision.\n\n8. TAKE NOTICE that unless the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with interest thereon is released within two months from the date of service of this notice, my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings against you and the State of Bihar for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages, and costs, without any further reference to you in the matter."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 87,50,000/- along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from 28.02.2026 till actual payment, and pay damages of Rs. 5,00,000/- for the wrongful withholding within a period of two (2) months from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings before the competent civil court, at your risk, cost, and consequences, without any further reference to you.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Anjali Verma\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. BCB/4521/2018\nChamber No. 42, Patna High Court Bar Association, Patna - 800001\n\n(Counsel for M/s Ganga Construction Pvt. Ltd.)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

event: checklist
data: {"items":["Send via Registered Post AD (Acknowledgement Due) — retain receipt","Send additional copy via Speed Post","Retain photocopy of notice with postal receipts","Keep proof of delivery (AD card) safely — needed at time of filing suit","Wait mandatory 2 months from date of receipt before filing suit","Attach all supporting documents referenced in the notice","Verify noticee's correct designation and office address"]}

